    excerpt: "Installing commercial solar in India involves technical, regulatory, and financial steps that most companies navigate blindly. This comprehensive checklist ensures nothing falls through the cracks.",
    category: "Implementation Guide",
    tags: ["commercial solar installation India", "solar installation process", "solar plant commissioning", "rooftop solar approval", "DISCOM solar"],
    author: { name: "Sanjay Kumar", role: "Head of Implementation", avatar: "SK" },
    publishedAt: "2024-05-20",
    readingTime: 13,
    coverImage: "solar-installation",
    content: `## Commercial Solar Installation in India: The Complete Process Guide

Installing a commercial solar system in India is a multi-phase project involving technical design, government approvals, DISCOM coordination, equipment procurement, civil and electrical work, and commissioning. Here's exactly what to expect — and how to avoid the most common delays.

### Overview: Typical Timeline for a 500kW Commercial Rooftop

| Phase | Duration | Key Activities |
|---|---|---|
| Site Assessment & Feasibility | 1–2 weeks | Shadow analysis, structural assessment, load profiling |
| Commercial Agreement | 2–4 weeks | PPA/CAPEX proposal, negotiation, signing |
| Design & Engineering | 3–4 weeks | Detailed engineering, equipment procurement order |
| Permits & Approvals | 4–8 weeks | DISCOM NOC, electrical inspector permit, net metering application |
| Procurement & Logistics | 4–6 weeks | Module, inverter, structure delivery |
| Civil & Electrical Work | 4–6 weeks | Mounting structure, cable laying, electrical panel |
| Commissioning & Testing | 1–2 weeks | System testing, DISCOM inspection, net meter installation |
| **Total** | **19–32 weeks** | |

### Phase 1: Site Assessment & Feasibility

**Technical Checklist**:
- [ ] Rooftop structural load-bearing capacity assessment (minimum 15–20 kg/m² for solar)
- [ ] Shadow analysis (3D modelling — check chimneys, AC units, parapets)
- [ ] Measurement of usable roof area (accounting for walkways, equipment clearance)
- [ ] Orientation and tilt assessment (south-facing preferred in India)
- [ ] Electrical load data collection (12 months of electricity bills)
- [ ] Grid connection point identification (LT/HT panel location)

**Output**: Feasibility report with system size recommendation, generation estimate (P50/P90), and preliminary cost estimate.

### Phase 2: Commercial Agreement

**For CAPEX Model**:
- Engineering, Procurement & Construction (EPC) Contract
- O&M Agreement (typically 5–10 year comprehensive AMC)
- Performance Guarantee terms (minimum generation guarantee)
- Payment milestone schedule

**For PPA/OPEX Model**:
- Power Purchase Agreement (15–25 year tenure)
- Rooftop Lease Agreement (if applicable)
- Performance and availability guarantees
- Exit and step-in rights

**Key legal provisions to verify**:
- [ ] Clear ownership of solar assets
- [ ] Comprehensive O&M responsibilities
- [ ] Performance guarantee with liquidated damages
- [ ] Insurance requirements clearly assigned
- [ ] Dispute resolution mechanism

### Phase 3: Design & Engineering

**Detailed Engineering Deliverables**:
- Single line diagram (SLD) — electrical layout
- Module layout drawing — exact panel placement on roof
- Structural drawing — mounting system design
- Cable schedule — sizing and routing
- Protection system design
- Earthing and lightning protection design

**Equipment Selection**:
- Modules: Tier 1 manufacturers preferred (Longi, JA Solar, Waaree, Vikram Solar)
- Inverters: String inverters for <100kW; central inverters for larger systems
- Mounting: Aluminium/GI structures (hot-dip galvanised)
- Cables: UV-resistant DC cables; conforming to IEC standards

### Phase 4: Permits & Approvals (The Critical Path)

This phase is typically the longest bottleneck. Navigate it proactively.

**Central/National**:
- [ ] MNRE approval (if claiming subsidies)
- [ ] ALMM compliance certificate for modules (if required)

**State/DISCOM Level**:
- [ ] Net Metering Application to DISCOM
- [ ] Technical feasibility approval from DISCOM
- [ ] Synchronisation approval
- [ ] Net meter installation request

**Local/Municipal**:
- [ ] Building plan approval (if structure exceeds permissible floor space)
- [ ] Fire NOC (for certain occupancies)
- [ ] Aviation clearance (if near airport)

**Electrical Inspector**:
- [ ] Electrical installation drawing approval
- [ ] Form 5 / Form 6 submission (varies by state)
- [ ] Inspection and testing certificate

**Pro Tips to Accelerate Approvals**:
1. Submit complete documentation in first attempt — incomplete applications restart 30-day timelines
2. Engage a local electrical contractor licensed with the DISCOM
3. Use a knowledgeable EPC partner with DISCOM relationship in your city
4. Follow up weekly — DISCOM queues are long, proactive follow-up matters

### Phase 5: Equipment Procurement

**Procurement Checklist**:
- [ ] Purchase order with delivery schedule
- [ ] Pre-shipment inspection (PSI) for large orders
- [ ] Insurance during transit
- [ ] Delivery acceptance and quality inspection (visual, performance testing)
- [ ] Component serialisation for warranty tracking

**Common Procurement Mistakes to Avoid**:
- Ordering equipment before DISCOM approval (risk of delay = storage costs)
- Accepting modules without datasheet verification
- Not specifying IEC certification requirements

### Phase 6: Civil & Electrical Installation

**Quality Checkpoints**:
- [ ] Structural bolt torque specifications verified
- [ ] Module inter-row spacing for cleaning access
- [ ] DC cable crimping and termination quality
- [ ] String open-circuit voltage testing before inverter connection
- [ ] Earthing resistance testing (<5 Ω)
- [ ] Junction box IP rating verification

**Safety Requirements**:
- [ ] Safety harness requirement for all roof workers
- [ ] Isolation and lockout procedures
- [ ] Fire extinguisher presence on site
- [ ] Documented safety induction for all workers

### Phase 7: Commissioning & Handover

**Commissioning Tests**:
- I-V curve testing for each string
- Thermal imaging of panels (identify hot spots)
- Insulation resistance testing
- Protection relay testing (anti-islanding)
- SCADA/monitoring system integration test

**Handover Documentation**:
- As-built drawings
- Equipment serial numbers and warranty certificates
- O&M manuals
- DISCOM approval letters and net meter readings
- Commissioning test reports

**First Month Monitoring**:
- Daily generation vs. forecast tracking
- PR (Performance Ratio) calculation (target >75%)
- Inverter efficiency logging
- Any snag list items resolved

### Post-Commissioning: Ongoing Monitoring

S³ Solar provides 24/7 monitoring via our digital platform for all projects we implement or finance:
- Real-time generation data
- Alert system for underperformance
- Monthly performance reports
- O&M ticket management

**[Connect with our Implementation team](/register)** for a site feasibility assessment or to onboard as an S³ Implementer partner.`,
